---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Route required by docs/website/03-functional-spec.md line 21: "/docs —
// Integration guide". /docs/quickstart is the guide itself; this page is an
// index over it, not a second copy. It links to exactly the pages that exist.
const pages = [
  {
    href: '/docs/quickstart',
    title: 'Quickstart',
    body: 'The integration guide: sign in for a session cookie, create an API key, make a streaming chat completion, and every error code you can get back.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Documentation — apikita"
  description="Integration guides for the apikita API: authenticate, create a key, and call the OpenAI-compatible endpoint."
>
  <article class="space-y-12">
    <header>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Documentation</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-ink-muted">
        How to integrate with apikita: the OpenAI-compatible endpoint at
        <code class="font-mono text-sm">POST /v1/chat/completions</code>, the
        session cookie the dashboard uses, and the API keys that authenticate
        programmatic calls.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {pages.map((page) => (
          <li class="rounded-lg border border-edge bg-surface-raised p-5">
            <a href={page.href} class="font-medium underline">{page.title}</a>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{page.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm text-ink-muted">
        The quickstart is the only guide published so far. Nothing else is listed
        here rather than linked to a page that does not exist.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What the quickstart covers</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 max-w-2xl list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-ink-muted">
        <li>
          <strong>Authentication</strong> — sign in for an
          <code class="font-mono text-sm">HttpOnly</code> session cookie with
          <code class="font-mono text-sm">POST /auth/login</code>. The session
          cookie is for the dashboard only; it is never accepted on
          <code class="font-mono text-sm">/v1/*</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>API keys</strong> — scoped to a model allowlist, with their own
          spend limit and per-minute rate limit. The plaintext key is returned
          once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Requests</strong> — streaming over SSE and non-streaming JSON,
          with the terminal error event that ends a stream that failed mid-answer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Error codes</strong> — the full table, including which are worth
          retrying and where <code class="font-mono text-sm">Retry-After</code> is sent.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Elsewhere</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-ink-muted">
        Pricing is on the <a href="/#pricing" class="underline">landing page</a>.
        If you have not signed up yet,
        <a href="/signup" class="underline">create an account</a> — you will need
        one before you can create a key or top up the wallet.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
